{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792662387,"nonce":"rQOxsBUCfjFWxoIvIe7u6cssaIU=","title":"ci: make ci runs everything CI runs, and lefthook runs the fast checks on each commit","message":"`make ci` skips the web checks: they are written out in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (npm ci, typecheck, test, build), so a local `make ci` isn't the CI and CLAUDE.md has to list them apart. Lint, format and type-check should always run locally (the user, 2026-10-21), as co2-calculator's lefthook does.\n\nADR 0001 (docs/adr/0001-check-results-are-signed-git-notes.md) makes the local run the proof; the cycle protocol's M4 proposes `[cycle.checks]` from lefthook's pre-commit. This gives it a real one to read.\n\n\n- `make ci` runs the web checks and build too, and installs web dependencies only when the lockfile changed.\n- `ci.yml` sets up Go and Node, then runs `make ci`, and nothing else.\n- A `lefthook.yml` pre-commit runs gofmt, go vet and the web typecheck, each only when matching files are staged. No pre-push hook: wtx's push guard owns it.\n- lefthook is pinned and installed by one documented command.\n- CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and README say `make ci` alone.","files":null}]}